                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 2,
                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "The loss of Dr. Nolan Williams is a devastating one for the medical community, for veterans, and for anyone who believes in challenging the status quo to do what\u2019s right.\n\nNolan was a brilliant scientist. He was a fighter. Someone who refused to accept that the existing standard of care was good enough for those who\u2019ve served and suffered. He pushed boundaries because he saw what too many ignored: that veterans with TBI and PTSD weren\u2019t getting better, and something had to change.\n\nHis work with ibogaine gave many of our Special Operations veterans something they hadn\u2019t had in years\u2014hope. A second chance. Healing.\n\nI was honored to have Nolan as a guest on my podcast and as a speaker at last year\u2019s Health Care Innovation Summit. He brought an unmatched level of commitment to solving the invisible wounds of war.\n\nRest easy, Nolan.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1760553155,
                "view_count": 9561
