                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 11,
                "retweet_count": 8,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Here\u2019s what the adults are doing about healthcare:\n\n1) Expand access to health savings accounts (HSAs) for all Americans. Money should go to the patient, not insurance companies.\n\n2) Price transparency - you need to know prices for a market to work.\n\n3) Cost share reduction - we could actually both lower cost sharing and premiums. Democrats fought to get this provision out of the Big Beautiful Bill.\n\nI fought to add Direct Primary Care to the list of qualified expenses that can be paid for with a HSA in the Working Families Tax Cut. \n\nInsurance coverage and access to care are not the same thing. HSAs bridge that gap.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1763160877,
                "view_count": 11782
